          "content": "B) Take the $5,000\n\nThe decision rests on evaluating the overall balance of well-being and suffering. The marginal utility of the $5,000 is substantially higher for someone enduring months of intense financial anxiety, mounting penalties, and severe deprivation than it is for someone who absorbs the loss simply by delaying a luxury vacation without threatening their basic security. Because no innocent party will be falsely accused and no wider social instability is created by detection, the total net reduction in hardship outweighs the comparatively minor distress and inconvenience caused to the owner, resulting in a greater balance of overall welfare.",
